    <item>
      <title>Research</title>
      <link>https://ugoue.github.io/research/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 04 May 2023 14:17:37 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>https://ugoue.github.io/research/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;research-interests&#34;&gt;Research interests &lt;a class=&#34;header-link&#34; href=&#34;#research-interests&#34;&gt;&lt;svg class=&#34;fill-current o-60 hover-accent-color-light&#34; height=&#34;22px&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; width=&#34;22px&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M0 0h24v24H0z&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34;/&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M3.9 12c0-1.71 1.39-3.1 3.1-3.1h4V7H7c-2.76 0-5 2.24-5 5s2.24 5 5 5h4v-1.9H7c-1.71 0-3.1-1.39-3.1-3.1zM8 13h8v-2H8v2zm9-6h-4v1.9h4c1.71 0 3.1 1.39 3.1 3.1s-1.39 3.1-3.1 3.1h-4V17h4c2.76 0 5-2.24 5-5s-2.24-5-5-5z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Most of my research is in Graph Theory, but I am also very interested in problems lying at the intersection of Graph Theory and other areas. In particular, I like concepts related to Geometric Group Theory, Coarse Geometry or Topology.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A few topics I (am trying to) work on:&lt;/strong&gt; Cayley graphs, coarse graph theory, metric graph theory, cycle bases, geometric group theory, canonical tree-decompositions, twin-width, universal covering, evasiveness of graph properties, fractional colouring of graphs, diameter-degree problem, group tilings.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
